      "body": "## Summary of Changes\nFixed incorrect M-RoPE positions when chunked prefill splits a video placeholder (5-channel EVS path) inside the placeholder. The issue was that `recompute_mrope_positions()` didn't receive the placeholder offset and start_idx from the caller, causing wrong anchor calculations and write offsets.\n\n## Motivation & Context\nCloses #62969\n\nThe bug occurred with `--video-pruning-rate` on models using the 5-channel EVS path (Qwen3-VL and subclasses). When chunked prefill splits a video placeholder inside the placeholder, the function wrote wrong M-RoPE positions. This affected tokens of the chunk that starts mid-video, text tokens after the video, and the `mrope_position_delta` which shifts every decoded token.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix has been verified with the reproduction script provided in the issue. It correctly handles all 2-chunk split scenarios inside video placeholders for both layouts (with and without outer markers). The fix ensures that placeholder token `j` gets the correct `mm_pos[:, j] + (position of the token before the placeholder) + 1` regardless of chunk boundaries.\n- Gate Report: Python syntax compiled: vllm/multimodal/video_prune/evs.py; Python syntax compiled: vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_states/mm_pruning.py; Notice: Python tests had failures in tests/",
